WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.216 --> 00:00:02.048
- We're starting this
episode off in Houston

00:00:02.048 --> 00:00:04.128
because we just finished a pie episode

00:00:04.128 --> 00:00:06.496
and we were feelin' a little
bit of a late-night snack.

00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:07.690
Today on Worth It, we're gonna

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.597
be trying three different pho's

00:00:09.597 --> 00:00:11.465
at three drastically
different price points

00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:13.216
to find out which one is the most worth it

00:00:13.216 --> 00:00:14.116
at it's price.

00:00:14.116 --> 00:00:15.952
- And joining us on our adventure today

00:00:15.952 --> 00:00:18.895
is a very fun guy by
the name of Justin Yu,

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:20.747
owner of Theodore Rex.

00:00:20.747 --> 00:00:22.296
- [Steven] He's a local from Houston,

00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:23.485
James Beard Award winner.

00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:24.917
- [Andrew] Certainly knows his pho.

00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:27.564
He likes to grab a bowl of
pho after a hard day of work

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:28.877
and that's what we're gonna do with him,

00:00:28.877 --> 00:00:30.765
show us how it happens, late-night-style,

00:00:30.765 --> 00:00:31.677
in Houston.

00:00:31.677 --> 00:00:32.510
- Wow.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.885
It is midnight right now.

00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:36.591
The pho don't stop (laughing)

00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:37.548
when we walk in.

00:00:37.548 --> 00:00:39.826
- Is that a Kesha lyric
that you just turned

00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:41.004
into a pho pun?

00:00:41.004 --> 00:00:41.837
- Yeah.

00:00:41.837 --> 00:00:42.670
- [Andrew] Geez.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.896
(classy jazz) music)

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:47.678
- [Kevin] My name is Kevin
Pham, I am the proprietor

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:48.736
here at Pho Binh by night.

00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:50.101
We do authentic pho.

00:00:50.101 --> 00:00:51.616
4pm 'til 12am.

00:00:51.616 --> 00:00:53.147
On Fridays and Saturdays, we're open

00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:53.980
until 3AM.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.176
- Whoa.
- Whoa, really.

00:00:55.176 --> 00:00:56.205
- Where did you learn to make pho?

00:00:56.205 --> 00:00:57.576
- I've always wanted to learn it.

00:00:57.576 --> 00:00:59.576
It was like a secret
held away from me like

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:00.984
Mom telling you to close your eyes

00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:02.883
when there's a naked woman on TV.

00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:03.716
(laughing)

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:05.317
My grandfather flew from Vietnam

00:01:05.317 --> 00:01:06.495
because he's retired there,

00:01:06.495 --> 00:01:08.507
and I showed up every
day just to learn it.

00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:11.216
Then my step-dad would come
over and show me his way.

00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:13.624
Confusing at first, but
then I got the gist of it,

00:01:13.624 --> 00:01:14.685
developed my own way.

00:01:14.685 --> 00:01:16.706
The thing about pho is everyone
has their own preference.

00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:19.426
I like to eat bone marrow
and we never had it

00:01:19.426 --> 00:01:21.757
in our formula, and one
day, I was just like,

00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:23.395
"Hey, this is actually pretty good,"

00:01:23.395 --> 00:01:25.045
and I gave it to a friend.

00:01:25.045 --> 00:01:27.045
My friend actually was sitting with

00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:28.736
Alison Cook of the Houston Chronicle.

00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:30.797
A week later we're in
the Houston Chronicle

00:01:30.797 --> 00:01:33.323
for our bone marrow which we never sold,

00:01:33.323 --> 00:01:36.895
and that kinda boosted us the first year.

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:38.517
- I mean we walked in and
the first person we met

00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:39.522
was your wife?

00:01:39.522 --> 00:01:40.505
Is that right?
- Yeah.

00:01:40.505 --> 00:01:41.816
She's the great, if it weren't for her,

00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:43.275
man, this place would not last.

00:01:43.275 --> 00:01:45.107
Or I wouldn't last here, by myself.

00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:45.940
- [Steven] Why is that?

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.146
- The way we operate has
always been Ma 'n Pa.

00:01:49.146 --> 00:01:50.376
- How do you make your broth?

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.917
- [Kevin] Well it starts
off with the bones,

00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:53.856
the center piece and the joints.

00:01:53.856 --> 00:01:56.205
- [Steven] So it really is bone soup?

00:01:56.205 --> 00:01:57.157
- And brisket.

00:01:57.157 --> 00:01:59.476
When you look at BBQ pit masters,

00:01:59.476 --> 00:02:02.245
they're called pit masters,
what we do is similar

00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:05.399
to being called a pot master.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:07.957
That flame, it has to be low,

00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:10.365
you gotta simmer it and
cook the noodles first,

00:02:10.365 --> 00:02:12.467
strain it out, top off the meats,

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.005
and then you just go onions.

00:02:14.005 --> 00:02:15.237
- [Andrew] Pot master
thing, I've never heard

00:02:15.237 --> 00:02:17.259
of pot master--
- I kind of wanna be called

00:02:17.259 --> 00:02:18.855
that one day, so hey!
(laughing)

00:02:18.855 --> 00:02:20.180
- [Andrew] Yeah, I think
after this, you're gonna

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.467
be pot master for sure.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:22.517
All right, awesome.
- Actually, I did have

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.908
one last thing, sorry.
- Okay, Steven.

00:02:23.908 --> 00:02:26.485
- I notice you have this
thing goin' on here.

00:02:26.485 --> 00:02:29.760
- That's actually pickled
lemons to make Chanh Muoi.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.925
Pickled lemonade.

00:02:30.925 --> 00:02:33.100
- We are here with Chef Justin Yu.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.933
- Have you had this drink before?

00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:35.133
- I have.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.383
- All right, cheers! (dull clinking)

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:37.316
- To a nice bowl of pho.

00:02:37.316 --> 00:02:38.307
- Oh yeah,
- Whoo!

00:02:38.307 --> 00:02:39.498
- That is amazing.

00:02:39.498 --> 00:02:40.938
- This is kind of a
dead-ringer for Gatorade.

00:02:40.938 --> 00:02:42.298
Is that crazy?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.298 --> 00:02:43.237
Then I guess there's a good amount

00:02:43.237 --> 00:02:44.218
of salt in Gatorade, too.

00:02:44.218 --> 00:02:45.599
- So we ordered some pho.

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:47.446
Me and Andrew, kind of
like in high school,

00:02:47.446 --> 00:02:49.596
cheated off your exam?

00:02:49.596 --> 00:02:50.886
And we got your order.

00:02:50.886 --> 00:02:52.407
- Got it (laughing).

00:02:52.407 --> 00:02:54.476
So it's actually funny,
'cause I'd cheated off

00:02:54.476 --> 00:02:55.996
of somebody else's order. (laughing)

00:02:55.996 --> 00:02:57.316
It's called nam gau gan.

00:02:57.316 --> 00:02:59.184
Gau is the fatty brisket,

00:02:59.184 --> 00:03:00.665
and then gan is the tendon.

00:03:00.665 --> 00:03:02.738
To me it has all the perfect little bits.

00:03:02.738 --> 00:03:04.866
The reason why I love it
here is that they cut it

00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:06.583
almost perfect size every time.

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:08.877
So, to me you'd sip the broth first.

00:03:08.877 --> 00:03:11.236
That's the ringer for a really great pho.

00:03:11.236 --> 00:03:12.567
(slurping)

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.476
This one's such a clean broth,

00:03:14.476 --> 00:03:16.207
they've obviously taken a lot of time

00:03:16.207 --> 00:03:19.021
to either blanch the
bones or skim the bones.

00:03:19.021 --> 00:03:22.631
- It's like a meal and a
glass of water in one bite,

00:03:22.631 --> 00:03:25.127
'cause I'm both getting the savory bits,

00:03:25.127 --> 00:03:26.586
but I feel refreshed.

00:03:26.586 --> 00:03:27.936
How's that broth for you, Andrew?

00:03:27.936 --> 00:03:29.349
- Uh, it's (clicks tongue)

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:30.299
(laughs)

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:31.607
- That right there?

00:03:31.607 --> 00:03:33.058
The fatty brisket?

00:03:33.058 --> 00:03:34.276
- That fat hangin' off.

00:03:34.276 --> 00:03:36.375
- That's another level of flavor.

00:03:36.375 --> 00:03:38.424
- So for you is this
broth perfect right now

00:03:38.424 --> 00:03:39.386
or are you gonna--
- This broth is

00:03:39.386 --> 00:03:40.394
absolutely perfect

00:03:40.394 --> 00:03:41.227
right now.
- You're not gonna

00:03:41.227 --> 00:03:43.106
add anything, or--
- I love a good amount

00:03:43.106 --> 00:03:44.138
of cilantro.

00:03:44.138 --> 00:03:45.978
I like to have it with the stems, too.

00:03:45.978 --> 00:03:47.396
It's really all about that texture.

00:03:47.396 --> 00:03:48.933
Break it up so it's bite-sized.

00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:50.914
Thai basil. Some bean sprouts.

00:03:50.914 --> 00:03:52.392
I like my bean sprouts raw.

00:03:52.392 --> 00:03:53.258
- Ahh.

00:03:53.258 --> 00:03:55.178
- You got the bone marrow, and then add it

00:03:55.178 --> 00:03:57.167
to the little section I'm about to eat.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.146
And it's just so,

00:03:58.146 --> 00:04:00.394
because you'll get this punch of richness.

00:04:00.394 --> 00:04:02.494
- Maybe because it's late at night,

00:04:02.494 --> 00:04:03.739
just made a new friend,

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:05.966
but this may be my favorite food

00:04:05.966 --> 00:04:07.987
right now in the world.

00:04:07.987 --> 00:04:10.569
I love sushi, I love...

00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:11.654
what do I love, I love...

00:04:11.654 --> 00:04:12.874
I don't want to say asai bowls,

00:04:12.874 --> 00:04:13.707
because that's kind of...

00:04:13.707 --> 00:04:15.486
But I do love asai bowls!

00:04:15.486 --> 00:04:16.492
Little bit of shame there,

00:04:16.492 --> 00:04:19.580
but this is really hittin'
the spot for me right now.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.822
All right! (laughing)

00:04:20.822 --> 00:04:21.989
It is so late.

00:04:25.954 --> 00:04:27.554
(laughing)

00:04:27.554 --> 00:04:31.004
- Pho Binh hooked us up with
another specialty drink.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.062
- Artichoke tea.

00:04:32.062 --> 00:04:33.562
- Artichoke tea.

00:04:33.562 --> 00:04:34.940
- Another refreshing thing!

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.773
- (laughing) Another one!

00:04:35.773 --> 00:04:38.344
- So we're leaving Pho Binh By Night.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.625
- We're actually leaving by car.

00:04:40.625 --> 00:04:41.518
- And so was Justin.

00:04:41.518 --> 00:04:43.518
He actually is heading
off to his restaurant

00:04:43.518 --> 00:04:45.380
to clean up, now?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.413
- Yeah so our next stop
is actually in Hawa--

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:49.437
(light drum beat)

00:04:49.437 --> 00:04:51.176
Look at that.

00:04:51.176 --> 00:04:53.337
- [Steven] So we just had
some amazing pho in Houston,

00:04:53.337 --> 00:04:54.486
learned a lot from Justin,

00:04:54.486 --> 00:04:56.608
and now we've come to Honolulu,

00:04:56.608 --> 00:04:59.703
and we're gonna be
tryin' some delicious pho

00:04:59.703 --> 00:05:01.183
from a place called The Pig and the Lady.

00:05:01.183 --> 00:05:02.426
Three types of pho.

00:05:02.426 --> 00:05:04.077
- We're eating delicious soup,

00:05:04.077 --> 00:05:06.635
that's the soup from which all life comes.

00:05:06.635 --> 00:05:07.926
- There it is.

00:05:07.926 --> 00:05:10.464
(kitchy guitar music)

00:05:10.464 --> 00:05:11.844
- [Andrew] I'm Andrew.
I'm the chef-owner of

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.044
The Pig and the Lady restaurant.

00:05:13.044 --> 00:05:15.050
I'm gonna be giving
you guys our pho broth,

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.536
and we're gonna do three
different versions.

00:05:16.536 --> 00:05:18.106
One of them is the pho bac,

00:05:18.106 --> 00:05:19.696
which is our Northern-style beef pho.

00:05:19.696 --> 00:05:21.849
We also do seasonal broths, one of them

00:05:21.849 --> 00:05:22.816
is the duck pho.

00:05:22.816 --> 00:05:25.626
We also have a vegan option,
which we're really proud of.

00:05:25.626 --> 00:05:28.426
- Could you tell us a
little bit about the naming

00:05:28.426 --> 00:05:29.626
of The Pig and the Lady?

00:05:29.626 --> 00:05:31.494
- I'm the pig. I'm born
the year of the pig.

00:05:31.494 --> 00:05:33.323
And the lady is my mother,

00:05:33.323 --> 00:05:36.468
and also represent my
wife, my best friend.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:38.266
It was just a way to honor them.

00:05:38.266 --> 00:05:40.634
The beef pho, which
you'll be having first,

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:43.005
it's pho bac, so it's a Northern-style,

00:05:43.005 --> 00:05:44.776
pretty much the heart and
soul of the restaurant.

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:46.034
That's Mom's recipe.

00:05:46.034 --> 00:05:47.256
We don't mess with that.

00:05:47.256 --> 00:05:49.655
Fresh rice noodles, bun
tham bi rice noodle,

00:05:49.655 --> 00:05:51.144
they just make everything by hand.

00:05:51.144 --> 00:05:53.016
It just has a really nice texture.

00:05:53.016 --> 00:05:55.336
We get our beef from
Makaweli Ranch in Kauai.

00:05:55.336 --> 00:05:57.946
Typically we use round,
which is the shoulder part.

00:05:57.946 --> 00:06:00.438
It's a leaner type of
beef, but it's very tender.

00:06:00.438 --> 00:06:02.153
- [Steven] I've never
had pho like this before.

00:06:02.153 --> 00:06:05.140
I've always had it where you
get the vegetables on the side,

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.072
but here it's all done for you.

00:06:07.072 --> 00:06:08.506
And this is what I'm talkin' about!

00:06:08.506 --> 00:06:10.167
- This drink is called Cobra Commander.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.074
- Are we sharing?

00:06:11.074 --> 00:06:11.907
- Yeah.

00:06:14.566 --> 00:06:15.674
Ooh.
- Spicy.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:16.840
- Cutest thing I've ever seen.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.000
(laughing)

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.668
- Oh. Oh.
- Oh yeah.

00:06:19.668 --> 00:06:22.085
Cheers. Sliced beef shoulder.

00:06:23.286 --> 00:06:25.194
Wow! That's so tender!

00:06:25.194 --> 00:06:26.365
- Yeah, that's so good.

00:06:26.365 --> 00:06:27.742
- Adam, you should try the beef right now

00:06:27.742 --> 00:06:29.799
while it's still a little bit raw.

00:06:29.799 --> 00:06:30.632
Here you go.

00:06:30.632 --> 00:06:31.696
Wow!

00:06:31.696 --> 00:06:33.831
Adam just gave the wide-eyed look.

00:06:33.831 --> 00:06:34.764
Broth time?

00:06:34.764 --> 00:06:35.889
- [Andrew] Broth boys.

00:06:35.889 --> 00:06:38.915
(slurping)

00:06:38.915 --> 00:06:40.594
- I'm into that. Okay.

00:06:40.594 --> 00:06:41.663
I'm into that.
- Can I just put

00:06:41.663 --> 00:06:43.554
my straw in here, please? (laughing)

00:06:43.554 --> 00:06:44.616
- Go for it!

00:06:44.616 --> 00:06:46.616
- No, I'm not an animal.

00:06:49.982 --> 00:06:52.045
This is like a baptism for my mouth.

00:06:52.045 --> 00:06:53.544
- So you've been born again?

00:06:53.544 --> 00:06:54.384
In the name of pho.

00:06:54.384 --> 00:06:56.300
- My mouth has. (laughing)

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.703
- One of them is the duck pho.

00:06:57.703 --> 00:06:58.845
We get Mary's Ducks.

00:06:58.845 --> 00:07:01.024
We go ahead and that, we'll slice up

00:07:01.024 --> 00:07:02.845
the medium-rare poached duck breast,

00:07:02.845 --> 00:07:04.285
and we'll put the bones back in

00:07:04.285 --> 00:07:06.085
and cook that for a further eight hours.

00:07:06.085 --> 00:07:08.512
That allows all the duckiness to come out,

00:07:08.512 --> 00:07:10.514
and then fat renders out from the broth.

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:13.643
We'll save all of that duck
fat to finish the broth.

00:07:13.643 --> 00:07:15.916
We also put a poached egg yolk,

00:07:15.916 --> 00:07:19.729
it's an affordable luxury
that everybody loves.

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:21.029
- [Steven] Yolk time!

00:07:21.029 --> 00:07:22.633
(simultaneous groaning)

00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:23.760
Oh yes!

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.296
- [Andrew] I'm gonna duck
my duck with a duck yolk.

00:07:28.296 --> 00:07:31.026
- There's this word that
they use in Malaysia, 'jelak'

00:07:31.026 --> 00:07:33.496
and it means when something is so rich,

00:07:33.496 --> 00:07:35.386
that the more you eat
it, you get sick of it.

00:07:35.386 --> 00:07:37.335
And this is the anti-jelak.

00:07:37.335 --> 00:07:38.925
I wanna drink this bowl of pho,

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:40.743
and then I wanna eat another bowl tomorrow

00:07:40.743 --> 00:07:43.053
for breakfast, for lunch, for dinner.

00:07:43.053 --> 00:07:44.445
And just, for the rest of my life.

00:07:44.445 --> 00:07:47.266
- I just wanna spray this
broth on myself like cologne.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.529
- We also have a vegan
pho that we're featuring.

00:07:49.529 --> 00:07:52.666
It's a challenge in itself to
emulate the same experience

00:07:52.666 --> 00:07:54.885
that you would have
with a rich duck broth,

00:07:54.885 --> 00:07:56.136
or a rich beef broth.

00:07:56.136 --> 00:07:58.845
The broth is made with vegetable and kombu

00:07:58.845 --> 00:08:00.957
to give it depth, enoki
mushroom for meatiness,

00:08:00.957 --> 00:08:04.789
herb oil from thai basil, add
a little bit more lusciousness

00:08:04.789 --> 00:08:07.026
to the broth, that was
kind of our pet project,

00:08:07.026 --> 00:08:09.715
and this is the end result
of that, we're really stoked.

00:08:09.715 --> 00:08:11.976
- [Steven] This is the
one I'm most intrigued by.

00:08:11.976 --> 00:08:13.426
- Look how pretty this is.

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:15.316
- [Steven] Yeah, it's what I
want my garden to look like

00:08:15.316 --> 00:08:16.149
when I get older.

00:08:16.149 --> 00:08:17.697
- [Andrew] Yeah, soup garden.

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.088
- Drizzle.

00:08:19.088 --> 00:08:20.282
Sizzle.

00:08:20.282 --> 00:08:21.115
- [Adam] All right.

00:08:21.115 --> 00:08:22.865
Little bit of tomato.

00:08:24.826 --> 00:08:26.197
- That's wonderful. (laughing)

00:08:26.197 --> 00:08:27.030
- Oh my.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:30.186
It's extremely delicious,
but I've never had a tomato

00:08:30.186 --> 00:08:31.829
in this setting before.

00:08:31.829 --> 00:08:33.336
I'm just delighted.

00:08:33.336 --> 00:08:35.578
Adam's gone rogue.

00:08:35.578 --> 00:08:38.274
Chef Andrew said that this would be

00:08:38.274 --> 00:08:40.176
as satisfying as the other phos,

00:08:40.176 --> 00:08:41.784
and he's absolutely right.

00:08:41.784 --> 00:08:44.380
It's not so different.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.003
I'm suspicious he's cheating.

00:08:46.003 --> 00:08:47.205
(laughing)

00:08:47.205 --> 00:08:48.453
Was that great pho or what?

00:08:48.453 --> 00:08:49.843
- You were a vegan fiend.

00:08:49.843 --> 00:08:51.535
And now we've got some shaved ice.

00:08:51.535 --> 00:08:53.223
What flavors did you get on top?

00:08:53.223 --> 00:08:56.498
- I got a bad assembly, I
kind of got pee-snow colors.

00:08:56.498 --> 00:09:00.439
Coffee, lilikoi passion and creme brulee?

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:01.552
I don't think I'm doin' it right.

00:09:01.552 --> 00:09:03.999
- I got the strawberry,
the guava and the mango,

00:09:03.999 --> 00:09:04.940
and that's how you do it.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.019
- Look at this.

00:09:06.019 --> 00:09:07.256
Does it get better than this?

00:09:07.256 --> 00:09:08.814
Sunset. Ocean breeze.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:10.717
Icy refreshment.

00:09:10.717 --> 00:09:12.496
- We went from a port...

00:09:12.496 --> 00:09:13.801
To an island...

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:15.801
And now we head to Las--

00:09:16.967 --> 00:09:18.008
We're in Vegas!

00:09:18.008 --> 00:09:19.781
And specifically, we're in Chinatown.

00:09:19.781 --> 00:09:22.154
We're headed to our last location,

00:09:22.154 --> 00:09:24.545
but before we go there, I have a...

00:09:24.545 --> 00:09:25.765
Pho Fact!

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:29.825
In Seattle they have a challenge for pho,

00:09:29.825 --> 00:09:32.554
where you can eat an
entire massive bowl of pho

00:09:32.554 --> 00:09:34.887
in 90 minutes, you win $100.

00:09:35.988 --> 00:09:40.005
In that bowl of pho is
four liters of broth.

00:09:40.005 --> 00:09:41.234
- Four liters?!

00:09:41.234 --> 00:09:42.365
- (laughing) That's right.

00:09:42.365 --> 00:09:44.405
- You cannot consume that much liquid

00:09:44.405 --> 00:09:45.496
in one sitting.

00:09:45.496 --> 00:09:46.405
That's too much.

00:09:46.405 --> 00:09:48.594
I can't believe how far we've
come to make this video.

00:09:48.594 --> 00:09:49.427
- That's right, what--

00:09:49.427 --> 00:09:53.020
- Houston, Honolulu, to Las Vegas?

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.634
- But you know what I like about that?

00:09:54.634 --> 00:09:58.174
There's good pho all over America.

00:09:58.174 --> 00:10:00.448
People are doin' big things
all over the country.

00:10:00.448 --> 00:10:02.134
- Yeah, next time we'll
just have to actually

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.824
go to Vietnam.

00:10:03.824 --> 00:10:04.657
- Done.

00:10:04.657 --> 00:10:07.578
(funky jazz music)

00:10:07.578 --> 00:10:09.640
- Hi, my name is Khai Vu and I'm the owner

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:11.181
of District One Kitchen and Bar here

00:10:11.181 --> 00:10:12.489
in Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:10:12.489 --> 00:10:13.568
- Where does that name come from?

00:10:13.568 --> 00:10:15.876
- It comes from District
One in Ho Chi Minh City,

00:10:15.876 --> 00:10:17.697
and that's where I was born and raised.

00:10:17.697 --> 00:10:19.300
It have all kind of different food.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.931
People go there for
entertainment and dining.

00:10:22.931 --> 00:10:25.300
Today I will be serving
you guys a lobster pho.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.430
We fly our Maine lobster live from Maine.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:30.139
When the lobster get
here, we boil them, first,

00:10:30.139 --> 00:10:31.356
and then I'll take the shell

00:10:31.356 --> 00:10:33.150
and make a concentrated lobster base.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.300
We use the head to flash-fry them,

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.100
and we cook them in the broth

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.358
so it brings out more lobster flavor.

00:10:38.358 --> 00:10:40.750
And then I'll marry
that with the bone broth

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.889
from the original pho
that we cooked at dinner

00:10:42.889 --> 00:10:44.396
with the oxtail, the big bones,

00:10:44.396 --> 00:10:46.868
so you have a really
good broth from the bone

00:10:46.868 --> 00:10:48.038
and the lobster flavor.

00:10:48.038 --> 00:10:50.260
- And do we get other
items on the side or?

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.768
- Usually when people order the lobster,

00:10:51.768 --> 00:10:53.049
they have two - three people,

00:10:53.049 --> 00:10:55.078
so sometimes if people want surf 'n turf,

00:10:55.078 --> 00:10:56.278
we serve with a side of bone marrow,

00:10:56.278 --> 00:10:57.780
and we call it the Big Bone Soup.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:00.070
It's the bone marrow that we use

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.396
to cook the pho broth with.

00:11:01.396 --> 00:11:03.243
- [Steven] We're in Vegas, so.

00:11:03.243 --> 00:11:04.076
Baby.

00:11:04.076 --> 00:11:05.196
(clinks)

00:11:05.196 --> 00:11:06.317
- [Andrew] Look at that.

00:11:06.317 --> 00:11:09.070
You know when Godzilla
emerges from the sea?

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:09.958
- Oh ho, yes!

00:11:09.958 --> 00:11:12.790
- And he's coming up to
the city to destroy it,

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.620
and his head just pops out of the water?

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.350
(whooshes dramatically)

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.234
That's what this is like.

00:11:18.234 --> 00:11:19.329
- [Steven] All right, broth first.

00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:21.198
Seafood broth! Cheers.

00:11:21.198 --> 00:11:23.529
(clinks)

00:11:23.529 --> 00:11:25.779
(slurping)

00:11:28.822 --> 00:11:29.702
(tongue clicks)

00:11:29.702 --> 00:11:31.089
(laughing)

00:11:31.089 --> 00:11:32.582
- I'm surprised at how much you can taste

00:11:32.582 --> 00:11:34.564
the lobster in this.
- Whoo. Yeah.

00:11:34.564 --> 00:11:37.341
- Nothing makes you hungrier
than seeing a whole lobster...

00:11:37.341 --> 00:11:38.508
dead or alive.

00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:42.930
That's the good thing about lobster,

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.105
you don't...

00:11:44.105 --> 00:11:45.678
If you're gonna pay
this much for a lobster,

00:11:45.678 --> 00:11:48.517
I don't want you to sauce
up my lobster too much,

00:11:48.517 --> 00:11:50.950
just gimme the pure taste of lobster.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:51.900
It's like a steak.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.459
- I'm gonna make the perfect little bowl,

00:11:54.459 --> 00:11:56.631
get the lobster broth, get a little bit

00:11:56.631 --> 00:11:59.200
of this bone marrow, a
little bit of noodle,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.999
this is only if you zest.
- A little bit?

00:12:00.999 --> 00:12:01.922
There you go.

00:12:01.922 --> 00:12:03.005
Just a touch.

00:12:04.102 --> 00:12:06.352
(groaning)

00:12:07.691 --> 00:12:08.991
- When a soup makes you go,

00:12:08.991 --> 00:12:10.488
(contented groaning)

00:12:10.488 --> 00:12:13.243
after taking a big slurp of it...

00:12:13.243 --> 00:12:14.180
- Bone meat.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.431
- Bone meat is like, if
I was a Bond villain,

00:12:16.431 --> 00:12:17.678
and you were my henchman?

00:12:17.678 --> 00:12:18.827
Your name would be Bone Meat.

00:12:18.827 --> 00:12:19.751
- No.

00:12:19.751 --> 00:12:21.763
- Okay, if you were a Marvel superhero,

00:12:21.763 --> 00:12:22.687
your name would be Bone Meat.

00:12:22.687 --> 00:12:23.745
- Yes! That's right!

00:12:23.745 --> 00:12:24.969
- And I would be Broth Boy.

00:12:24.969 --> 00:12:26.540
- Let's go fight crime! (laughing)

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:28.036
- Born in a 'broth'el? No.

00:12:28.036 --> 00:12:29.987
- Noooooo no, no, no.

00:12:29.987 --> 00:12:34.013
We just had a bowl of
pho with a lobster in it,

00:12:34.013 --> 00:12:35.771
literally a lobster.

00:12:35.771 --> 00:12:37.247
Flew in from Maine.

00:12:37.247 --> 00:12:39.652
- A lobster flew in? Are his arms tired?

00:12:39.652 --> 00:12:42.469
- So, Andrew, which pho was the most

00:12:42.469 --> 00:12:43.650
worth it to you?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.483
- Are you ready for this?

00:12:44.483 --> 00:12:45.703
I bet you can't guess what I'm gonna say.

00:12:45.703 --> 00:12:46.536
- I know what you're gonna say.

00:12:46.536 --> 00:12:48.888
- The Pig and the Lady
was my Worth It winner.

00:12:48.888 --> 00:12:50.010
- What? No.
- Yeah.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:53.910
It was the best single-slurp
of broth I've ever had.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.787
- My Worth It Winner
was Pho Binh By Night.

00:12:55.787 --> 00:12:57.128
- Wow, I did not see that coming.

00:12:57.128 --> 00:12:57.961
- [Steven] Really?

00:12:57.961 --> 00:12:59.135
- [Andrew] Yeah.
- And you know what?

00:12:59.135 --> 00:13:02.036
That night, I dreamed
about the fatty brisket.

00:13:02.036 --> 00:13:04.618
What's your Worth It Winner?

00:13:04.618 --> 00:13:06.661
Pig and the Lady?!
- Adam picks Pig and the Lady!

00:13:06.661 --> 00:13:07.802
(Whoops)

00:13:07.802 --> 00:13:08.762
- I knew that was comin'.

00:13:08.762 --> 00:13:09.882
- [Andrew] It's like a
cow and a lobster went

00:13:09.882 --> 00:13:10.954
in a hot tub together.

00:13:10.954 --> 00:13:13.654
(laughing)

00:13:13.654 --> 00:13:15.321
And I got to eat it.

00:13:16.485 --> 00:13:18.000
- [Steven] (laughing)
That coulda went weird.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.021
And I'm glad you didn't.

00:13:19.021 --> 00:13:21.539
I'm glad it ended there.
- Oh...it went weird.

00:13:21.539 --> 00:13:22.750
In the best way possible.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:23.583
- Oh yes.

